# Kernel-materialised secrets — these live in the CC `secrets` table and are written into
# Library/processes/secrets/ at runtime by pete-session-bootstrap.py / railway-bootstrap.py.
# They must NEVER be committed. The whole Library/ tree is runtime-materialised
# (secrets + helper symlinks) — the repo tracks no Library/ content, so ignore it all.
Library/

# Knowledge / plan / data TRANSPORT files. Plans, lessons, notes etc. are authored as a throwaway
# .md UNDER these logical paths inside the working tree (e.g. Projects/<proj>/files/<plan>.md) only so
# cc-knowledge-ingest.py records a clean vault_path; the real home is the CC `vault_notes` DB row and
# the file is discarded. They must NEVER be committed: the hourly `knowledge-reindex` cron re-ingests
# any .md it finds under these roots, so a committed transport file RESURRECTS a plan you deleted from
# the DB an hour later (the Xhale incident, 28 Jun 2026 — swept in by a catch-all `git add` on 26 Jun).
# The repo tracks no content under any of these roots — same rule as Library/ above.
Projects/
Daily/
Personal/
Businesses/
Customers/
Suppliers/
Properties/
Accreditations/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local caches / scratch
*.cache.md

# Materialised SECRETS, wherever they land. The rule above ignores Library/ because that is where
# pete-session-bootstrap.py is supposed to write them -- but on 4 Aug 2026 a work clone
# (/tmp/pbs-fix) was found with 41 credential files sitting at the REPO ROOT instead: live Xero
# tokens, Stripe keys, Supabase service-role keys, Odoo logins. Untracked and unignored, so a
# single `git add -A` would have committed the lot.
#
# Relying on every tool writing to the right folder is not a control. These patterns make the
# LOCATION irrelevant: a secret file is ignored wherever it is dropped. The originals live in the
# CC `secrets` table and are re-materialised every session, so nothing is lost by ignoring them.
*-keys.json
*-key.json
*-graph.json
*-tokens.json
*-credentials.json
*-api.json
*-oauth-client.json
*-service-account.json
*-sentry.json
*-ga4.json
*-gtm.json
*-cookieyes.json
*-wordpress.json
*-login.json
*-vercel.json
*-indexnow-key.json
*-web-analytics.json
stripe-*.json
